  "reason": "Evidence: The best-performing configuration so far is config_002 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + concat, acc=0.629), and all completed experiments use avgpool aggregation—no transformer aggregation has been tested. This is a major unexplored design axis. Question: Does transformer-based aggregation improve over simple avgpool when combined with the strongest known encoders (PCA + ViT)? config_042 changes exactly one variable (avgpool → transformer) relative to config_002, cleanly isolating the aggregation effect. Why best next: With a limited budget, testing a single high-impact unexplored dimension on the current best backbone maximizes information gain. A positive result identifies a new best configuration and confirms aggregation matters; a null result rules out an entire family of transformer-aggregation variants, saving future experiments. This is more informative than testing fusion (weighted vs. concat) because we already have weak evidence that fusion differences are small (~1-2%), whereas aggregation is completely untested and could have a larger architectural impact."
}

